   "notes": "From HTML v1: Qwen2.5-7B SFT backbone, one all-linear LoRA (r=8; 196 modules, 1,568 rank slots) shared by 3 round-robin agents (≤6 turns); router picks top-392 slots per role-turn segment (hard mask + centered gate [0.5,1.5]); GRPO with turn-aligned credit; role library induced offline (supervised encoder + K-means). Relevant to the user's 'no pre-assigned roles' idea: roles are induced from trajectories rather than hand-assigned, and the team's shared weights are the substrate. Content control: YES — random role prompt (MuSiQue 16.5/28.0 EM/F1) and shuffled induced role (8.5/19.1) are both far below ExRole, i.e., mismatched role conditioning hurts. Cross-family: no. Long-horizon/SWE: no (multi-hop QA). Shared structure: all agents read/write the same LoRA during training; routing = learned slot masks per role-context; conflicts handled only implicitly by slot separation; no test-time update, so no staleness. Safety: none. No code link on arXiv page.；训练方式：RL+SFT",
